00:18:07.000 --> 00:19:02.000
for signs of a lone elderly camper. While beginning their investigation into Russell Hill's disappearance, the police came across a tip that had been reported several days earlier. A man named Andrew Marquardt had notified authorities that he'd come across a burnt out campsite on Saturday March 21, the morning after Russell was last heard from. On Saturday March 28, the day after Russell was reported missing, officers set off for Buck's camp to follow up on the lead. What they found confirmed their worst fears – a white Land Cruiser matching Russell's. The campsite itself was a wasteland of twisted metal and ash, covering a precise three metre square. In the middle were the charred remnants

